+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The package creates ${SYSCONFDIR}/aimap.conf from the example, and the empty
directories ${SYSCONFDIR}/aimap and ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/mail/aimap. Three things
remain before aimap can serve mail.

TLS certificate and key
=======================

aimap reads /etc/ssl/aimap.crt and /etc/ssl/private/aimap.key unless
"tls certificate" and "tls key" in aimap.conf name others. See
aimap.conf(5).

Accounts
========

Mail accounts are not system users. Each is a line in two table(5) files,
${SYSCONFDIR}/aimap/credentials and ${SYSCONFDIR}/aimap/userbase, with a
maildir under ${LOCALSTATEDIR}/mail/aimap. The EXAMPLES section of aimap.conf(5)
creates both files and adds an account.

Mail delivery
=============

smtpd(8) can deliver into the same maildirs and read the same two files.
See "Mail delivery" in aimap.conf(5).

Then enable and start the daemon:

    # rcctl enable aimap
    # rcctl start aimap
